A||N||9||Vlad||What can be the reason of EGR code (32).||||5||
Z||000000||Vlad||09-11-2000||03:16 AM||||Hello.<P>I am getting a code 32 while driving with a speed more then 55 m/h. The EGR valve is good, EGR solenoid was replaced yesterday, there are no vacuum leaks.<P>What else can cause this code to come up??<P>Thanks<P>Vlad<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||09-11-2000||09:48 AM||||<BR>The tube that runs off the egr valve probably has a hairline crack.<P>I replaced the solenoid, the valve, have no vacuum leaks (that i know of anyway) and still receive the 32 code.<P>The tube is all that is left for me, and I have read several times that the tube developes weaknesses and eventually crack causing 32 problems.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||09-11-2000||12:30 PM||||I had the same problem and did the same things.  I finally replaced the tube that was originally broken that I had tried to fix with JB weld.  I found the JB weld held on pretty good but developed small hairline cracks that probably caused the codes.  Check junkyards and e-bay for tubes.  You should be able to pick one up for less than $25 or you can get the cure all stainless steel flexible one for $99.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||09-11-2000||01:35 PM||||The actual code is cause by the switch in the control solenoid not grounding the test pin back to the ECM. When vacuum is present this switch closes to ground.<P>Obviously, the switch can be bad (not terribly unusual), but the common causes are vacuum leaks that bleed vacuum off that line.<P>EGR tube, vacuum hoses, or big leaks elsewhere.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||09-11-2000||04:32 PM||||I've been getting intermittant 32 code errors this year.  EGR valve was replaced prior to the codes.  I could nail the code coming out when I was on the highway usually running 70 and going up a hill.  But still intermittant.  The car still ran great with the check engine light on.<P>I've started replacing the vacuum lines around the cruise control module and the coffee can.<P>I drove 300 miles + on Saturday, no check engine engine light.  Is it fixed ??? ||||reg||3
Z||000005||AL||09-11-2000||08:31 PM||||i was gettig code 32 also,i replaced the soloniod and replaced all vac hses with rubber ones have not had code 32 for over a year.thank god.<B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gokart||09-11-2000||08:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Old Lar:<BR><B>I drove 300 miles + on Saturday, no check engine engine light.  Is it fixed ??? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It wants you to THINK it's fixed Old Lar! Then one day after your complacent enough not to bother looking at the dash...WHAM <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">"service eng soon"<BR>I have a new solenoid, valve, thoroughly checked the tube(had it off), vaccum lines and leaks and have the right gaskets for all of them and still get 32 when I hit 75/80 mph. I've just learned to live with it and haven't noticed ANY ill effects because of it. Gokart'sgirl fix is: Stop going over 75 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> What fun is that <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||8
Z||000007||Spyro86SE||09-12-2000||04:34 PM||||i have the same 32 code once i hit over 55mph the light will go on and it stays on till i turn the car off i still have to change the solenoid and hoses so i hope this will solve the problems and if not baboom goes the car ||||reg||12
Z||000008||jfuredy||09-13-2000||07:44 PM||||Yeah, it sucks when you can't find the cause of the problem, but believe me, it's worth fixing.  When code 32 gets set the ECM goes to a default timing mode that reduces the advance, reducing your power.  The ECM even remembers that this code was set after you stop the car and restart it, even though the light isn't on yet.  The only way to reset it is to unplug the power to the ECM.<P>When I fixed my EGR solenoid and reset my computer it was the best thing I had done to my car so far.  It had about as much effect as when I just recently replaced my original cat with an aftermarket one.<P>I think it's worth fixing.<BR>Joe Furedy<BR>'88 Formula<BR>Phoenix, AZ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Gokart||09-13-2000||08:56 PM||||So do I Joe, but what do I replace/fix next! I didn't know the default timing mode and it being a power throbber <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> I'm sure I don't speak for myself when I say "I'm just fed up with 32" and honestly I haven't noticed any ill effects, but wonder if I would if I could find the prob! Maybe I got a defective solenoid from the Fiero Store? Not knocking them because they are great, but I'm sure I wouldn't be the only one that bought a defective product!<P>Marc 87GT||||reg||1
